# The arm `gq3` seeds: each a GQ 3 ground truth, in the surface #1316 ships
# (`match { … } where`, commas), with one injected error of one refusal
# class, refused by the front door with `code`. Ported on 2026-11-19 from the
# 2026-11-11 seeds (their `where`-arm conversion on gq3/variant-match-where):
# three classes are refusals no more and are dropped (a minus spaced on one
# side only, e3-11; a reserved edge name written bare, e3-16; a space before
# a call's parenthesis, e3-28), e3-15's class is inverted, since a write
# body in `match { }` is now the write's form, and three codes move:
# e3-03 (`fuzzy` is refused as a function, T6, before its positional budget),
# e3-17 (`where` inside the braces, Q017) and e3-21 (`= null`, T7).
# On 2026-11-19, re-judged on #1316's head after its admitted spellings
# (`case … end` in any letter case, `||`, `<>`, single quotes and keywords in
# any letter case are non-canonical spellings the front door accepts, lint
# `L212` to `L216`): two more classes are refusals no more and are dropped,
# `CASE … END` (e3-10) and an uppercase keyword (e3-22).

--- seed
id: e3-01
task: t03
class: infix `contains` and `starts_with` (edition 2's spelling)
code: T7

--- text
query titled() {
  match { $d: Doc }
  where $d.title contains "graph" and $d.title starts_with "The"
  return { $d.title }
}

--- seed
id: e3-02
task: t05
class: `contains` over a list property (edition 2's spelling)
code: T7

--- text
query tagged() {
